WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.935
-Our first guest tonight,

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.403
hosts Sunday TODAY with
Willie Geist

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.603
Sunday mornings on NBC.

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.338
He also co-hosts
Morning Joe,

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:08.140
weekday mornings on MSNBC.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.010
Please welcome back to the show
Willie Geist, everybody.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.478
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:31.163 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:32.698
Nice to have you back, man.
-Hey man. How are you?

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.600
Good. You shared
a very nice moment

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.934
with me as we
were walking out.

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.937
You said your makeup
was also very bad during COVID.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.038
-I was watching the monologue.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.874
My first interview
I did during COVID.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:44.310
I had people call me after
and saying prayers up.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.311
You have COVID.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.645
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:48.181
-That's how bad you looked.
-That's how bad it was.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.950
And I, like you, appreciate our
makeup artist so much more.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.119
-Yes. Well,
you also took advantage

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.753
of both makeup and wardrobe

00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:57.356
because the Halloween
on The TODAY Show,

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:58.691
this is a tradition.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.460
This is the highest bar.
I'm going to --

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:06.231
This is I'm not just being
a Homer NBC guy.

00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:07.433
-Well, here's our secret.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.101
We have an amazing team
at The TODAY Show,

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.404
plus a group
you know well --

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:15.308
the SNL costume,
hair, makeup, wardrobe,

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.543
the wigs,
the whole show, so.

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:19.412
-Two years ago, we actually
had you on this same day,

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.580
two years ago,
you've been Tom Brady.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.515
You upped your game
this year, my friend.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.351
You were Harry Styles.
-I was Harry Styles. Yeah.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.853
-And and there --
there's a photo

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.920
of Harry Styles right there.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.355
And you're just really...

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.456
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:31.691
...really going for it.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.791
-That angle.

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.293
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.828
-This is, uh...

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.663
-Oh, wow. Wow.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:39.632
-This is a tall
Harry Styles.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.866
-[ Laughing ] So tall.
-So tall.

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:43.903
-Tall and not quite as lean
as Harry Styles.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.972
-Now, were your colleagues
impressed?

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.907
Do you get feedback
when you show up on set

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.109
from the other
TODAY show team?

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.609
-It's a very supportive
environment

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.144
because everybody's putting
themselves out there.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:53.479
-And a lot of times when you're
putting it out there

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.982
on The TODAY Show,
that out there is outside.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.383
-Outside.
-A lot of the show is outside.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.384
-It is.
-It is not the summer.

00:01:59.384 --> 00:02:00.586
-No, it's not the summer.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.488
So you first of all,
we get out there

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.457
at 5:00 a.m. to rehearse.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.192
-And then the big show
is about 8:00.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.192
So it's, you know.

00:02:07.192 --> 00:02:08.728
It's late October.
-Yeah.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.997
-It's 40 degrees
or something like that.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.099
I have a skintight jumpsuit on

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.933
with diagonal stripes.
-Yeah.

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:16.102
-In the commercial break,

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:19.071
[Laughing] Al Roker,
Al Roker came up to me

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:21.440
and started reading
the weather on my body.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.441
And by that
I mean he goes,

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:24.577
"Ooh, it's awfully
chilly up here."

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.978
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:30.083
And then he says, "And
unseasonably cool down here."

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.884
-How dare he.
How dare he.

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.587
-Isn't that mean?
-Meteorology comedy, it's done.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.189
-Yeah, at work, it's a cliche.
-You also, you --

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.524
Look, this wasn't just costume,
you know,

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.226
again, a lot of the best people

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.961
put their best
into the way you looked.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.297
You then matched that effort
with your dance moves.

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.466
Can we -- Can we talk
a little over this video

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.033
of what you're having here?
-Yes, let's see what you have.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.002
Oh, Gosh.
-I mean, that's really good.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.303
You're lip-synching.
-Is it?

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:54.240
-That's the lip-synching part.
So, Harry Styles...

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.875
-There's a real good
Harry Styles move right here

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.009
at the end that I.

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.578
-Yeah. You know
I see it on playback.

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:00.813
-There it is.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.583
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.551
There it is.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.053
-Really? Yeah?

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.655
I don't know.

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.857
I spent a lot of time
in the days

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:14.360
leading up
to Halloween on YouTube

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.263
with Harry Styles dance moves,
to the point my kids are like,

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.366
"Dad, are you still watching
Harry Styles dance?"

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.202
And I pulled out, I think,
he has three big moves.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.571
First, we're just going
big energy like a fist pump.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:26.839
-Yeah, he does the fist pump.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.407
-And then on this song,
as it was,

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:31.610
I noticed he does a big
like a reverse windmill thing.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.479
-Yeah.
-So that's number two.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.949
And then the last one you saw
there was big on Instagram

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:39.551
I think, where he does like
he's in here a little bit

00:03:39.551 --> 00:03:40.853
and he's leaned back.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.589
And the crowd screams.
-I accidentally watched it once.

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:45.157
-Accidentally.
-And I feel like the algorithm

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:46.525
is like, hey,
you want to see that every day?

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:47.593
-I know.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:48.995
Imagine me.
-Yeah.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.463
-I spent two days watching.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.731
the FBI's going
to seize my computer.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.731
-I feel like for our
professional job

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:53.900
sometimes we have
to watch stuff.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.634
I once a month,
I'd like to have a meeting

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.002
with the algorithm people
and be like,

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:58.237
"Hey, that's not me."

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.172
-No, that was for work.

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:02.675
-That was a thing for work.
-Yes, clear all.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.077
-And, yeah, every time
I'm going to watch it.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.580
But that doesn't mean I want you
to keep giving it to me.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.014
-That's the thing.
That's the thing.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:10.883
You reject it
and then you just lean into it.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.418
-Yeah.
-You just accept that you can't.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.987
-Like, I guess I am
who you are telling me I am.

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:16.623
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:19.125
I mean, every now and then,
because this one did, I think,

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.293
maybe go a little bit
more viral than a normal

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:22.728
"TODAY Show" segment.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:25.097
Did you hear from anybody
who you realize maybe isn't

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:26.966
watching the show every day,
but saw it on social media?

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.035
-Oh, my gosh, I -- So my
daughter had a game yesterday.

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.939
She plays field hockey.
We go to the visiting field,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.607
which means I don't know
the parents.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:38.076
I walk in, walk past
a group of moms

00:04:38.076 --> 00:04:40.513
and they all go,
"Hi, Harry." Yeah.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.914
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.549
And I was like,
oh, this is my legacy.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.583
Yeah, this is it.

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:45.685
-You did all this.
-This is how...

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.186
-All this work
and that's your legacy.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.822
-It's been a long road and this
is all I'll be remembered for.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:52.158
-Well, I do want to talk
to you about the other stuff

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.693
I think you should be
remembered for.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:56.095
We'll be right back with more
from our friend Willie Geist.

